1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:05,550
Same vendor, same treasury. Two outcomes.

2
00:00:06,767 --> 00:00:14,567
MissionPay secures agent treasuries. Owner signs limits,
contract enforces on Avalanche.

3
00:00:15,767 --> 00:00:23,237
Three objects govern payouts: signed policy, Merkle
proof, and Treasury gate.

4
00:00:24,433 --> 00:00:29,233
The allow list drained funds to an off mission vendor.

5
00:00:30,433 --> 00:00:37,093
On Avalanche Fuji, Mission Pay strictly reverted with
zero funds lost.

6
00:00:38,300 --> 00:00:43,780
Each row links to a real Fuji transaction receipt.

7
00:00:44,967 --> 00:00:50,787
In judge mode, live Fuji receipts prove on-chain
behavior.

8
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:58,940
Testing an attacker. The contract strictly reverts with
payee not in mission set.

9
00:01:00,133 --> 00:01:07,313
Testing the owner address succeeds. Read-only simulation
requires zero gas.

10
00:01:08,500 --> 00:01:14,830
Copy the cast command to query public avalanche fuji rpc
directly.

11
00:01:16,033 --> 00:01:20,793
Updating the mission merkle root requires the owner's
signature.

12
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:28,590
Prompt injection tricks the agent, but our dual layer
guard protects the treasury.

13
00:01:29,800 --> 00:01:34,850
Tainted from tool output, our validator blocks the
payout.

14
00:01:36,067 --> 00:01:44,387
Snowtrace confirms live execution reverted on Fuji with
payee not in mission set.

15
00:01:45,600 --> 00:01:55,280
Cryptographically anchored on Fuji, ERC-8004 validation
confirms a perfect score.

16
00:01:56,467 --> 00:02:01,407
Tamper one byte and the cryptographic hash chain breaks.

17
00:02:02,600 --> 00:02:09,090
Restore the original, and 100% cryptographic integrity
is confirmed.

18
00:02:10,300 --> 00:02:17,140
Agents propose payouts while Avalanche smart contracts
enforce limits.

19
00:02:18,333 --> 00:02:23,973
LLMs can be fooled. Budgets on Avalanche cannot.
